users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8","state":"uploaded","size":3727,"digest":"sha256:7e455496a2040a2a7fa61e3154b7a827baadbbe70388a2519bac7d35542fe97b","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-10-27T00:09:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T00:09:09Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/weft/releases/download/v0.4.55/v0.4.55.md"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DocumentDrivenDX/weft/tarball/v0.4.55","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DocumentDrivenDX/weft/zipball/v0.4.55","body":"---\nddx:\n  id: weft.release-0.4.55\n  type: release-notes\n  activity: deploy\n  status: draft\n  authoring:\n    home: repo\n  links:\n    - id: weft.release-0.4.54\n      kind: informed_by\n    - id: CONTRACT-003\n      kind: informed_by\n    - id: TP-001\n      kind: informed_by\n---\n\n# Weft 0.4.55\n\n## Release scope\n\nThis candidate changes the Python distribution name from `weft-sql` to\n`umf-weft`. The Python import remains `weft`; compiler protocols, backend\nregistrations and SQL behavior retain the qualified 0.4.54 compiler base,\nincluding G02 and the integrated Unity/raw-read fixes. Version and distribution\nmetadata change, so every released wheel requires fresh qualification.\n\nPublication remains pending until the hosted producers, immutable GitHub release,\nPyPI OIDC upload and public byte checks pass. The generated `release-pins.json`\nwill bind the exact source, workflow runs, wheel bytes and native-module bytes.\nNo note embeds its own commit hash.\n\n## Audience and channels\n\nPython consumers and dependency maintainers receive the change through the\nGitHub release and PyPI project. Hosts retain responsibility for execution,\ntransactions, authorization and their own installed-package admission gates.\n\n## Changes and fixes\n\nThe release uses Actions for all three wheel targets: Linux x86_64, Linux ARM64\nand macOS ARM64. The macOS producer checks the installed wheel and compares nine\nfrozen refusal responses across Rust, installed Python and real Chromium WASM.\nLinux producers check exact installed packaging only. No sdist is produced.\nThe existing gated PyPI workflow publishes the qualified bytes using OIDC.\n\nThe selected wheel composition retains `WFT-BACKEND-VERSION` for the three\nolder Databricks requests and `WFT-BACKEND-MISSING` for the other six vectors.\nThe generic corpus's default-registry expectations remain unchanged; the\nproducer checks this selected composition and requires complete Rust/Python/WASM\nresponse-byte parity.\n\n## Breaking changes and required actions\n\nNew dependency declarations must use `umf-weft==0.4.55` after publication. Keep\n`import weft` and existing protocol identifiers unchanged. Replace the old\ndistribution in a fresh environment; do not install both distributions together,\nbecause they provide the same import package. Existing immutable `weft-sql`\nreleases and consumers pinned to them retain their original names and evidence.\n\n## Migration or rollback guidance\n\nConsumers remain pinned until the new public archive hashes match the qualified\nGitHub assets and their owning integration gates pass. To hold an upgrade,\nretain the previously qualified environment and dependency pin. Recreate that\nenvironment to roll back; do not overwrite a released wheel or relabel an old\nreceipt as evidence for this distribution.\n\n## Known issues and support\n\nThe nine macOS vectors establish refusal-response parity only. They do not\nqualify positive query compilation or native PostgreSQL execution. Linux checks\nestablish packaging identity only. Separate compiler/native evidence retains its\noriginal versions, source and scope; this release adds no production executor,\nmanaged database, generated-client or security authority claim. Consumer\nadmission and a public fresh-install check are separate gates.\n\n## References\n\n- [Previous release scope](../../04-build/releases/v0.4.54.md)\n- [Compile/host boundary](../../02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-003-compile-and-host-boundary.md)\n- [Project test plan](../../03-test/TP-001-compiler-conformance.md)\n- [Hosted ARM64 producer](../../../../.github/workflows/release-hosted-macos.yml)\n- [Three-platform promotion](../../../../.github/workflows/release.yml)\n- [PyPI publisher](../../../../.github/workflows/publish-pypi.yml)\n"}